  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore (Co. Down) Urban District Council, nine seats. Results printed in the Belfast News-Letter, 21 May 1955, p. 6 (BNA copy; read on the page image). The poll date is not stated in the report; the round stays on the calendar's urban polling day, 18 May 1955. The paper names eight of the nine elected; the ninth elected member (an Official Unionist) is not named in any source found. Searched: INA Belfast News-Letter and Irish News 25 Apr-30 May 1955 ('Dromore Urban', Dromore on the nomination and result pages of 5, 6, 19 and 20 May); BNA Belfast News-Letter 5-6 May 1955 nomination round-ups; BNA searches 'Dromore urban council nominations', 'Dromore urban council election' (all titles) and 'Dromore urban' (Banbridge Chronicle) for 28 Apr-15 Jun 1955."
